# Format: `path/glob  # reason`. Every entry MUST carry a reason; the script
# refuses to run otherwise. This list is a ROLLOUT SCHEDULE, not a set of
# permanent exemptions: each entry means "the fork hunks in this file are not yet
# annotated", and the list is meant to shrink. Removing an entry is the definition
# of done for bringing a file under the convention.
#
# A file leaves this list one of two ways:
#
#   1. CONVERGE — make it byte-identical to upstream/main, retiring it as a
#      drop site forever. Only when our delta is genuinely not worth carrying.
#   2. MARK — put a `# Fork:` comment inside every diverging top-level
#      definition saying what deviates and why, or a fork boundary banner if the
#      fork content is a contiguous tail block.
#
